{
  "requirement": "Saving encodes the completed result using its Serde JSON representation and\npreserves the dependencies captured in `Fingerprinted`.\n`Record`, `Dependency`, and `Fingerprint` support\nSerde when their type parameters do. The graph's node\nidentities and edge labels need not implement Serde unless its storage backend\nrequires those bounds.\n\n```rust,ignore\n#[non_exhaustive]\npub struct Record<N, L = ()> {\n    pub version: Option<CriterionVersion>,\n    pub dependencies: Vec<Dependency<N, L>>,\n    pub output: Value,\n}\n\nimpl<N, L> Record<N, L> {\n    pub fn new(\n        version: Option<CriterionVersion>,\n        dependencies: Vec<Dependency<N, L>>,\n        output: Value,\n    ) -> Self;\n}\n```\n\nTrait implementations\n\n```rust,ignore\nimpl<N: Clone, L: Clone> Clone for Record<N, L>;\nimpl<N: Debug, L: Debug> Debug for Record<N, L>;\nimpl<'de, N, L> Deserialize<'de> for Record<N, L> where N: Deserialize<'de>, L: Deserialize<'de>;\nimpl<N, L> Serialize for Record<N, L> where N: Serialize, L: Serialize;\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no adequacy gap in the reviewed tests for `requirements.sdk.graph.evidence.record`. Each obligation maps to a test with assertions:\n\n- **Saving encodes the completed result as Serde JSON.**\n  - `tests/storage.rs#fn[records_round_trip_and_malformed_or_incompatible_data_is_an_error]` stores `Record<String>` through `FileEvidenceStorage`. It reloads the record and asserts that `version`, `dependencies` and `output` are equal.\n  - `fn[storage_preserves_completed_answers_containing_credential_shaped_text]` checks that the output round-trips exactly and appears in the stored file.\n  - `fn[record_preserves_the_stored_version_encoding]` asserts the exact wire form for a `Some` version and for `None`.\n  - `tests/contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` asserts that the stored `output` JSON equals `{\"satisfied\":false,...}` and `null` for the two stored criteria.\n- **Dependencies captured in `Fingerprinted` are preserved.**\n  - In `fn[records_round_trip_and_malformed_or_incompatible_data_is_an_error]`, the `record` helper carries a `Dependency::Node` and a `Dependency::OutgoingEdges`, each with a `Fingerprint`. Dependencies are asserted equal after reload.\n  - A second record with a non-unit label (`\"tests/é\"`) is also reloaded and its dependencies asserted equal.\n  - `tests/contracts.rs#fn[input_checking_and_execution_keep_separate_observations]` asserts that the stored record's dependencies are exactly `Dependency::Node(Node(2), Fingerprint::new(\"text-v1\",\"after\"))`.\n  - `fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` asserts that records with no reads store empty dependencies.\n- **`Record`, `Dependency` and `Fingerprint` support Serde when their type parameters do.**\n  - The round trip with `String` nodes and `()` or `String` labels exercises both directions.\n  - Loading with the wrong parameter types (`u8` node, `u8` label) yields `FileStorageError::Json`.\n  - Malformed JSON gives a `Json` error.\n  - `fn[failed_serialization_preserves_records_and_failed_replacement_cleans_up]` checks that a `BadNode` whose `Serialize` fails produces a `Json` error and leaves the old record intact.\n- **Node identities and edge labels need not implement Serde.**\n  - `tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` uses opaque `Identity` and `Label` types with `Record` and `store_evidence`/`load_evidence`. That test is marked as testing this requirement.\n- **Type shape and trait implementations.**\n  - `Record::new` and the public fields `version`, `dependencies` and `output` are used directly in these tests.\n  - `fn[records_support_clone_and_debug_with_independent_bounds]` calls helper functions bounded only by `N: Clone, L: Clone` and by `N: Debug, L: Debug`. It asserts that the cloned fields equal the originals and that the Debug output contains the output text.\n  - `Serialize` and `Deserialize` are covered by the round-trip tests above.\n  - `tests/public_api.rs#fn[public_exports_match_the_appendix]` covers the export inventory.\n\nI did not find an assertion for `#[non_exhaustive]`. A compile-fail check is not a behavior the text requires to be tested, so I do not count this as a gap.\n\nThe clone and debug helper searches were closed after I relied on their snippets.",
